    "items": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Lo, mine eye hath seen all this,",
          "Mine ear hath heard and understood it."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "What ye know, the same do I know also:",
          "I am not inferior unto you."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Surely I would speak to the Almighty,",
          "And I desire to reason with God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But ye are forgers of lies,",
          "Ye are all physicians of no value."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "O that ye would altogether hold your peace!",
          "And it should be your wisdom."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Hear now my reasoning,",
          "And hearken to the pleadings of my lips."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Will ye speak wickedly for God?",
          "And talk deceitfully for him?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Will ye accept his person?",
          "Will ye contend for God?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Is it good that he should search you out?",
          "Or as one man mocketh another, do ye so mock him?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He will surely reprove you,",
          "If ye do secretly accept persons."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Shall not his excellency make you afraid?",
          "And his dread fall upon you?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Your remembrances are like unto ashes,",
          "Your bodies to bodies of clay."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Hold your peace, let me alone, that I may speak,",
          "And let come on me what will."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Wherefore do I take my flesh in my teeth,",
          "And put my life in mine hand?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Though he slay me, yet will I trust in him:",
          "But I will maintain mine own ways before him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He also shall be my salvation:",
          "For an hypocrite shall not come before him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Hear diligently my speech,",
          "And my declaration with your ears."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Behold now, I have ordered my cause;",
          "I know that I shall be justified."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who is he that will plead with me?",
          "For now, if I hold my tongue, I shall give up the ghost."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Only do not two things unto me:",
          "Then will I not hide myself from thee."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Withdraw thine hand far from me:",
          "And let not thy dread make me afraid."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then call thou, and I will answer:",
          "Or let me speak, and answer thou me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "How many are mine iniquities and sins?",
          "Make me to know my transgression and my sin."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Wherefore hidest thou thy face,",
          "And holdest me for thine enemy?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Wilt thou break a leaf driven to and fro?",
          "And wilt thou pursue the dry stubble?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For thou writest bitter things against me,",
          "And makest me to possess the iniquities of my youth."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Thou puttest my feet also in the stocks,",
          "And lookest narrowly unto all my paths;",
          "Thou settest a print upon the heels of my feet."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "And he, as a rotten thing, consumeth,",
          "As a garment that is moth eaten."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
